00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:32.680
Teams choosing between hosted APIs and self-hosted models can review the distinctions before committing to a deployment path. Okay, let's pop the hood on benchmark drift detection.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:43.240
Production APIs show measurable day-to-day variation that single-point evaluations miss. The mechanism runs the same prompt set repeatedly under fixed parameters.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:05:00.560
Computes daily medians then applies change point detection only when movement exceeds historical within-day noise. This approach adds roughly 5-10 times the evaluation cost of a one-time benchmark but surfaces sustained degradation masked by stochastic sampling.

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:14.920
The 31,000 score study confirmed between day swings three times larger than same-day noise. When the gap between daily medians crosses a minimum effect threshold, the system flags the model as degraded or recovering.

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:26.880
Use continuous monitoring when routing traffic across providers or when token cost differences justify switching. Skip it for one-off experiments where a single benchmark snapshot suffices.

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:34.220
The common gotcha is treating every score movement as signal before subtracting the expected daily variance floor.

